target: internal/golden/golden.go
verify: go test ./internal/golden/ -count=1 -run 'TestAMissingGoldenFailsAndNeverSkips'
expect: want failed and not skipped
why:    a missing golden must FAIL, because `go test` reports a skip as success and a skipped parity case guards nothing. CI greps the push and report logs for SKIP, so this variant is also caught there — but only in CI, and only for those two packages.
--- old
		t.Fatalf("no frozen oracle output for this case: %v", err)
--- new
		t.Skipf("no frozen oracle output for this case: %v", err)
